CMake: find libpng and libjpeg on iOS

OSG's top-level CMakeLists looks for libjpeg, libpng (and giflib,
libtiff) only when not on Apple, because macOS reads images through
ImageIO. On CMake's iOS platform that silently skipped the png plugin,
which OpenMW needs. Search them for iOS too; the recipe passes the
paths of the libraries built here (giflib and libtiff are not found).
macOS and the legacy OSG_BUILD_PLATFORM_IPHONE builds are unchanged.

Upstream: not submitted.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -820,9 +820,9 @@
 # potentially redundant modules.)
 
 # Image readers/writers depend on 3rd party libraries except for OS X which
-# can use Quicktime.
+# can use Quicktime. Builds for CMake's iOS platform use the libraries too.
 IF(NOT (ANDROID AND OSG_FIND_3RD_PARTY_DEPS))
-    IF(NOT APPLE)
+    IF(NOT APPLE OR IOS)
         FIND_PACKAGE(GIFLIB)
         FIND_PACKAGE(JPEG)
         FIND_PACKAGE(PNG)
